Subject: [PATCH 0/3] qcom: tolerate a bootloader-rewritten root compatible
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

DRAFT ONLY — not sent; human review and DCO sign-off required.

The OnePlus 8 Pro stock boot chain overlays the root compatible on every
boot, dropping qcom,sm8250. Peripheral compatibles remain intact. This
series avoids adding the vendor codename to Linux machine-match tables.

Keep existing root matches first, preserving board-specific UBWC choices
and all existing PD inventories. For an unmatched root, SM8250 may select
its SoC-wide UBWC and PD tables through qcom_smem_get_soc_id(). Unknown
IDs retain the unsupported-platform result. SMEM readiness is already
required by UBWC; PD mapper propagates probe deferral through its auxiliary
probe and now depends on QCOM_SMEM for valid built-in/module linkage.

The independent cpufreq change checks all matching controller nodes and
excludes cpufreq-dt if any is enabled. It depends on DT availability,
not driver probe order. Existing machine blocklists remain unchanged.

The local revert of the DO-NOT-UPSTREAM alias patch is deliberately not
included. Apply these three patches to the clean combo-equivalent tree.

Build and device validation status is recorded in KONA-ROOT-DESIGN.md.
No Tested-by, Signed-off-by or runtime success is claimed by this draft.
The owner must add their DCO sign-off after reviewing and testing.

